If you're familiar with OpenGL or D3D, these flags aren't new to you. They define {\i how}  the final color value of a pixel is computed, basing on the previous color at that pixel and the new color value from the material. The blend formula is: {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid SourceColor * SourceBlend + DestColor * DestBlend\par
}
 where DestColor is the previous color in the frame-buffer at this position and SourceColor is the material color before the transparency calculation.\par
 This corresponds to the {\b AI_MATKEY_BLEND_FUNC} property. \par
}{\par
{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
Enumerator:\par}
