{
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Defines all shading models supported by the library. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Property: {\b AI_MATKEY_SHADING_MODEL}\par
The list of shading modes has been taken from Blender. See Blender documentation for more information. The API does not distinguish between "specular" and "diffuse" shaders (thus the specular term for diffuse shading models like Oren-Nayar remains undefined). \par
 Again, this value is just a hint. {\b Assimp} tries to select the shader whose most common implementation matches the original rendering results of the 3D modeler which wrote a particular model as closely as possible. \par
}{\par
{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
